# Verification

Every meaningful change should have a proportionate verification strategy.

- Prefer the narrowest fast check first, then broaden to affected integration or end-to-end checks.
- Add or update tests when behavior changes or a defect would otherwise regress silently.
- Reproduce bugs before fixing when feasible; preserve the regression case.
- Use typechecks, linters, formatters, unit tests, integration tests, and smoke tests according to the project.
- Report exactly what was run, what passed, what failed, and what was not run.
- Never weaken a test merely to make the suite green without explicit justification.
